claim.claim-text:
41. A method of multiple channel high throughput purification of multiple samples from a chemical library, comprising of separating and purifying the components of each sample along a first channel by: moving the first sample to be separated into components along the first fluid path which passes through a separation medium that results in differential passage times through the separation media for the various components of the first sample; detecting individual components of the first sample as the first sample travels along the first fluid path; 

 identifying the components as associated with the first channel; sampling each component and sending a sample to a common analyzer with its channel identifier; determining if the analyzed sample meets the first selected sample characteristics; if the detected component of this first sample meets the selected sample characteristics a control valve is activated to allow collection of this first component in a first collector associated with the first channel; if the detected component of this first sample does not meet the selected sample characteristics a control valve is activated to direct the collection of these components to a second collector associated with the first channel; moving the second sample to be separated into components along the second fluid path which passes through a separation medium that results in differential passage times for the various components of the second sample; detecting individual components of the second sample as it travels along the second fluid path and identifying these components as associated with the second channel; sampling each component and sending such sample to a common analyzer with its channel identifier; determining if the analyzed sample meets the second selected sample characteristics; if the detected component of this second sample meets the selected sample characteristics a control valve is activated to allow collection of this second component in a first collector associated with the second channel; if the detected component of this second sample does not meet the selected sample characteristics the control valve is activated to direct the collection of these components to a second collector associated with the second channel; moving the third sample to be separated into components along the second fluid path which passes through a separation medium that results in differential passage times for the various components of the third sample; detecting individual components of the third sample as it travels along the third fluid path and identifying these components as associated with the third channel; 

 sampling each component and sending such sample to a common analyzer with its channel identifier; determining if the analyzed sample meets the third selected sample characteristics; if the detected component of this third sample meets the selected sample characteristics a control valve is activated to allow collection of this third component in a first collector associated with the third channel; if the detected component of this third sample does not meet the selected sample characteristics the control valve is activated to direct the collection of these components to a second collector associated with the third channel; moving the fourth sample to be separated into components along the fourth fluid path which passes through a separation medium that results in differential passage times for the various components of the fourth sample; detecting individual components of the fourth sample as it travels along the fourth fluid path and identifying these components as associated with the fourth channel; sampling each component and sending such sample to a common analyzer with its channel identifier; determining if the analyzed sample meets the fourth selected sample characteristics; if the detected component of this fourth sample meets the selected sample characteristics a control valve is activated to allow collection of this fourth component in a first collector associated with the fourth channel; if the detected component of this fourth sample does not meet the selected sample characteristics the control valve is activated to direct the collection of these components to a second collector associated with the fourth channel.

42. A multiple channel, high throughput supercritical fluid chromatographic purification system for substantially simultaneously purifying multiple samples from a chemical library, each of the samples being separable into first and second components comprising: a sample analyzer that analyzes selected sample characteristics; 

 a first purification channel coupled to the sample analyzer, the first purification channel including; a first chromatographic sample separation device positioned to separate a first sample flow into first and second sample components; a first detector positioned to detect the first and second components in the first sample flow; a first flow diverting device moveable to direct a sampling of the first sample component to the analyzer and the remainder of the first sample portion flows along a first flow path away from the diverting first flow device; a first collector positioned to receive at least a portion of the first or second sample component of the first sample the sample analyzer identified as having selected sample characteristics; a second collector positioned to receive remaining components of the first sample not having the selected sample characteristics; and a second purification channel coupled to the sample analyzer, the second purification channel including: a second chromatographic separation device positioned to receive a second sample flow for separation into the first and second components of the second sample flow; a second detector positioned to detect the first and second components of the second sample flow; a second flow diverting device moveable to direct a sampling of the first or second components to the analyzer and a remainder of the second sample portion flows along a second flow path away from the flow diverting device; a third collector positioned to receive at least a portion of the first or second sample components of the second sample having the selected sample characteristics; and 

 a fourth collector positioned to receive remaining components of the second sample not having the selected sample characteristics.
